-- title:
--   Residues of the Gauss prolongation as ratios of chart residues
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma\le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ contain the translation matrix `ModularGroup.T`, let $k_0\subseteq K_1\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ be intermediate fields, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $A_1$ a valuation subring of $K_1$ with $x\in A_1$ exactly when $x\in A$ (so $A_1=A\cap K_1$), assumed to be a discrete valuation ring, and assume the map sending $a\in A_1$ to the residue in $\kappa(A)$ of its image in $A$ is surjective. Let $K$ be the $K_1$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(K_1)$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the field [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) of ratios of $q$-expansions of integral modular forms for $\Gamma$, with $K$ an $A_1$-algebra compatibly with $A_1\subseteq K_1\subseteq K$, and let $E$ be the corresponding field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$. Let $\bar F$ be a field extension of the residue field of $A$ and $R$ a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ to $E$ with residue field $\bar F$ (a valuation subring $\mathcal O_R=R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $E$ whose trace on $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is $A$, together with a surjective residue homomorphism $\mathcal O_R\to\bar F$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, extending the residue map of $A$, and with the stated existence of scalings with nonzero residue), and assume $\mathcal O_R$ is given by the Gauss presentation: $f\in\mathcal O_R$ iff there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with the coefficientwise residue of $y$ nonzero and $f\cdot y=x$ coefficientwise in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$. Let $T$ be a field that is an $A_1$- and $K_1$-algebra compatibly, $j_T\in T$ nonzero and transcendental over $K_1$, with $T$ finite-dimensional and separable over $K_1(j_T)$; let $e:K\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }T$ be a ring isomorphism fixing $A_1$, carrying $e^{-1}(j_T)$ to the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{coeffEmb}_{K_1}(j_q)$ of the modular invariant, and let $\psi:T\to E$ be a ring homomorphism which on $e(K)$ is the coefficientwise extension of $K_1\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Then, for the chart algebra of elements of $T$ integral over $A_1[j_T]$ and equally for that of elements integral over $A_1[j_T^{-1}]$: for every $g\in\bar F$ there are $a,b$ in the chart algebra with $\psi(a),\psi(b)\in\mathcal O_R$, with the residue of $\psi(b)$ nonzero, and $g\cdot R.\mathrm{residue}(\psi(b))=R.\mathrm{residue}(\psi(a))$.
--
--   This is the statement that the residue field of the Gauss-type prolongation of $A$ to the modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ consists of quotients of residues of functions coming from the two affine charts ($j$ and $j^{-1}$) of the integral model of the level field $T$ over $A_1$. It supplies the fractions-of-residues input to the per-point analysis of stalks and étale coordinates on the two-chart integral model at full level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_chartAlg_residue_mul_eq_residue_of_coe_eq_coeffMap_of_residue_surjective.lean

